: "step_06", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_07", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_08", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_02", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_10", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_11", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_13", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_16", "role": "confounder_control"}], "narrative": "Structurally there is no direct 60->908 edge (step_12); the only short candidate route found is 60->29->904->908 (steps 06,07,08 confirm each hop exists, 3 hops, one single event per hop). However, none of the available tools expose event timestamps, so I could not verify that these three events occur in increasing time order inside [30939,69338] with successive gaps <= 600. Confounder checks argue against assuming a cascade: the mediator 904 is a global hub (380 events, 308 partners, 1769 incident triangles; step_10, step_11, step_13), so a static path through it is expected by chance regardless of timing, and 60 and 908 are themselves low-volume nodes with no repeat edges (step_02). A rough order-of-magnitude estimate for two independent 600-unit gaps plus correct ordering within the ~38k-unit window is ~4e-5 (step_16), i.e. an untimed structural path is weak evidence. Verdict: temporal evidence is unavailable/inconclusive rather than positive."}, "raw_final_response": "```json\n{\n  \"task_id\": \"t_1bd39123\",\n  \"decision\": \"insufficient\",\n  \"mechanism\": \"cascade\",\n  \"entities\": [60, 908, 29, 904],\n  \"window\": [30939, 69338],\n  \"confidence\": 0.55,\n  \"evidence\": [\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_12\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_09\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_05\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_06\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_07\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_08\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_02\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_10\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_11\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_13\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_16\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"}\n  ],\n  \"narrative\": \"Structurally there is no direct 60->908 edge (step_12); the only short candidate route found is 60->29->904->908 (steps 06,07,08 confirm each hop exists, 3 hops, one single event per hop). However, none of the available tools expose event timestamps, so I could not verify that these three events occur in increasing time order inside [30939,69338] with successive gaps <= 600. Confounder checks argue against assuming a cascade: the mediator 904 is a global hub (380 events, 308 partners, 1769 incident triangles; step_10, step_11, step_13), so a static path through it is expected by chance regardless of timing, and 60 and 908 are themselves low-volume nodes with no repeat edges (step_02). A rough order-of-magnitude estimate for two independent 600-unit gaps plus correct ordering within the ~38k-unit window is ~4e-5 (step_16), i.e. an untimed structural path is weak evidence. Verdict: temporal evidence is unavailable/inconclusive rather than positive.\"\n}\n```", "total_input_tokens": 45716, "total_output_tokens": 5644, "total_tokens": 51360, "total_latency_ms": 97230, "llm_calls": 9, "schema_repairs": 0, "status": "success", "error": ""}